Patch 7923: ps3_ppu_thread_ctx, the live register context of a PPU thread slot (rollback).

Symptom (two-copy rollback tests, with the clock, the audio and the sound server already following the game tick): the sound library's
server thread keeps its loop values in registers while it sleeps. A rollback restores guest memory, not those registers, so after a
rollback the thread went on with the values of the undone timeline and its timers fired 2-8 ticks apart on the two copies, depending
on each copy's own rollback history.

Now: ps3_ppu_thread_ctx(tid) returns the slot's context (NULL when the slot is not alive). The port copies the registers of every
helper thread parked in an HLE wait at each snapshot commit, and writes them back at a rollback to each thread that is parked in the
same wait (same call site) again.

diff --git a/runtime/syscalls/sys_ppu_thread.c b/runtime/syscalls/sys_ppu_thread.c
index 78d8a90..ed3a0ab 100644
--- a/runtime/syscalls/sys_ppu_thread.c
+++ b/runtime/syscalls/sys_ppu_thread.c
@@ -1516,6 +1516,16 @@ int ps3_ppu_thread_view(uint32_t tid, uint64_t* out, char* name)
 
 /* Patch 7916 (rollback netcode, read only): the callee-saved register file of one PPU thread slot: io[0..17] = r14..r31, io[18] = lr, io[19] = ctr, io[20] = cr,
  * io[21] = r1. `set` must be 0: a write request returns 0 (there is no write path). Returns 1 when the slot's thread is alive, else 0 and io is untouched. No lock. */
+/* J-Stars patch 3006 (rollback): the live register context of one PPU thread slot (NULL when the slot is not alive). The port copies the
+ * context of helper threads parked in a wait at every snapshot commit and writes it back at a rollback when the thread is parked in the
+ * same wait again: a loop's registers (a sound server's last time, a counter) are not in guest memory, which the snapshot restores. */
+ppu_context* ps3_ppu_thread_ctx(uint32_t tid)
+{
+    if (tid == 0 || tid > PPU_THREAD_MAX) return 0;
+    ppu_thread_info* t = &g_ppu_threads[tid - 1];
+    if (t->state != PPU_THREAD_STATE_RUNNING && t->state != PPU_THREAD_STATE_DETACHED) return 0;
+    return &t->ctx;
+}
 int ps3_ppu_thread_regs(uint32_t tid, uint64_t* io, int set)
 {
     if (set) return 0;   /* read only: there is no write path */
